"The top view shows the interferometer on an optical table: a light source focused to a point just before the beam splitter, the compensator plate, the movable mirror M₁ on a micrometer stage, the fixed mirror M₂ with two tilt screws, a gas cell {#} cm long in the M₂ arm, and the screen. The second picture is the screen itself, {#} mm across, with a millimeter scale.",
"The micrometer reads the mirror’s position to {#} μm. Turn it with its slider, the step buttons, by dragging the drum in the picture, or with the arrow keys.",
"A fringe counter (a photodiode at the center of the screen) adds one for each bright fringe that passes, whichever way it moves. Zero the counter starts it again and remembers the micrometer reading. A new light source, or putting the cell in or taking it out, cannot be counted.",
"The gas cell has a pump and a needle valve. Pump out takes it to {#} Pa; Let air in lets air back at about {#} kPa/s; Closed stops either. The gauge reads to {#} kPa.",
