"The room’s air is dry, at {#} °C and {#} kPa. Air’s index comes from Ciddor’s formula (Applied Optics, {#}) and is taken in proportion to the gas density: at constant temperature, \\(n - 1\\) is proportional to the pressure.",
"The laser lines are perfectly sharp. White light has a daylight spectrum, so its fringes appear only within about a micrometer of equal paths.",
